{"schema":"steinsaltz-glosses/v1","ref":"Zevachim 77b","word_index":"gemara tokens with a Hebrew letter, counted within the ☆ segment","sources":{"en":"William Davidson Edition - English (Koren Noé, Steinsaltz), Sefaria, CC-BY-NC","he":"Steinsaltz on Talmud, William Davidson Edition - Hebrew, Sefaria, CC-BY-NC"},"review":{"tractate":"Bekhorot","sample":"review/sample_v2.json","reviewer":"model (not human adjudication)","phrase_exact":0.86,"phrase_within_edge_word":1.0,"word_gloss_exact":0.71,"hebrew_scope_exact":0.9},"segments":[{"k":"1cc2f72e374c","n":22,"p":[[0,3,"Rav Huna says:"],[3,5,"on the cornea of the eye."],[5,6,"And … in accordance with","<b> And</b> his ruling is <b>in accordance with</b>"],[6,8,"of Rabbi Akiva,"],[8,9,"who says"],[9,10,"if"],[10,11,"ascended"],[11,13,"they shall not descend"],[13,18,"Say that Rabbi Akiva says"],[19,22,"after the fact, … Does … say … <i>ab initio</i>?","<b>after the fact,</b> meaning that if the priest already brought up the limbs of these blemished animals, they do not descend from the altar. <b>Does</b> Rabbi Akiva <b>say</b> that one may burn a mixture of these limbs <b><i>ab initio</i>?</b>"]],"w":{"1":"Rav","2":"Huna says","3":"on the cornea of the","4":"eye","5":"And … in accordance with","6":"of Rabbi","7":"Akiva","8":"who says","9":"if","10":"ascended","11":"not","12":"they shall … descend","13":"Say","14":"that","15":"Rabbi","16":"Akiva","17":"says","19":"after the fact … ab initio","20":"Does","21":"say"},"g":[[3,4,"כעין קרום","m"],[4,6,"ועל פי שיטת","a"],[13,14,"אמור","a"],[17,19,"שאם כבר עשה","a"],[20,21,"האם","a"]]},{"k":"6c8a2ce27a1f","n":15,"p":[[0,3,"Rav Pappa says:"],[3,6,"What are we dealing with here?"],[6,7,"where"],[7,10,"brought up upon"],[10,11,"ramp."],[11,13,"If so,"],[13,14,"even"],[14,15,"as is,"]],"w":{"0":"says","1":"Rav","2":"Pappa","3":"here","4":"What … with","5":"are we dealing","6":"where","7":"brought up","8":"upon","10":"ramp","11":"If","12":"so","13":"even","14":"as is"},"g":[[2,6,"כאן במה אנו עוסקים","a"],[11,13,"אם כך","a"],[13,15,"בעינם, כמות שהם","a"]]},{"k":"a92b19e2dacb","n":16,"p":[[0,1,"Rather,"],[1,4,"the reason of Rabbi Eliezer"],[4,6,"the Merciful One excludes … it is","<b>the Merciful One excludes</b> certain cases. After listing the various disqualifying blemishes, the verse states: “Neither from the hand of a foreigner shall you offer the bread of your God of any of these, because their corruption is in them, there is a blemish in them; they shall not be accepted for you” (Leviticus 22:25). This teaches that <b>it is</b>"],[6,7,"a blemish"],[7,11,"in them that they shall not be accepted;"],[11,12,"but"],[13,16,"by means of a mixture they shall be accepted."]],"w":{"0":"Rather","1":"the reason","2":"of Rabbi","3":"Eliezer","4":"the … excludes … it is","5":"Merciful One","6":"a blemish","7":"in them","9":"that … not","10":"they shall … be accepted","11":"but","13":"by means of","14":"a mixture","15":"they shall be accepted"},"g":[[1,2,"טעמו","a"],[5,6,"הכתוב","a"],[11,12,"אבל","a"]]},{"k":"794b1ec32faa","n":17,"p":[[0,1,"And the Rabbis, … It is","<b>And the Rabbis,</b> how do they expound this verse? The Gemara explains that they expound it as follows: <b>It is</b>"],[1,2,"blemish"],[2,6,"in them that they shall not be accepted;"],[6,7,"but"],[7,9,"blemish has passed,"],[9,10,"they shall be accepted."],[10,12,"And Rabbi Eliezer"],[12,13,"from … <i>bam</i>, … “<i>bahem</i>,”","<b>from</b> the previous clause in that same verse: “Because their corruption is in them [<i>bahem</i>].” Since the verse could have stated the shorter form of <b><i>bam</i>,</b> and instead stated <b>“<i>bahem</i>,”</b>"],[13,14,"And … the Rabbis,","<b>And</b> as for <b>the Rabbis,</b>"],[14,17,"they do not interpret … <i>bam</i> … “<i>bahem</i>”;","<b> they do not interpret</b> anything from the variation between <b><i>bam</i></b> and <b>“<i>bahem</i>”;</b>"]],"w":{"0":"And the Rabbis … It is","1":"blemish","2":"in them","4":"that … not","5":"they shall … be accepted","6":"but","7":"has passed","8":"blemish","9":"they shall be accepted","10":"And Rabbi","11":"Eliezer","12":"from … bam … bahem","13":"And … the Rabbis","14":"they do … interpret … bam … bahem","15":"not"},"g":[[0,1,"וחכמים","a"],[6,7,"אבל","a"],[13,14,"וחכמים","a"],[15,17,"אינם דורשים","a"]]},{"k":"e96ebdefa8ec","n":25,"p":[[0,4,"If that is so,"],[5,6,"view … the Merciful One permits","<b>view</b> the flesh of the limbs of the blemished animals as though they are pieces of wood? After all, <b>the Merciful One permits</b>"],[6,9,"speaking to … in accordance with their statement,","<b>speaking to</b> the Rabbis <b>in accordance with their statement,</b>"],[9,10,"According to my"],[10,12,"the Merciful One permits"],[12,13,"according to your"],[13,15,"at least agree with me"],[15,19,"flesh of a blemished"],[19,20,"is considered like wood,"],[20,22,"just as is"],[22,25,"flesh of a sin offering"]],"w":{"0":"If","1":"that is so","5":"view … the Merciful One permits","6":"speaking to … in accordance with their statement","9":"According to my","10":"the Merciful One","11":"permits","12":"according to your","13":"at least agree with","14":"me","16":"flesh","17":"of a","18":"blemished","19":"is considered like wood","20":"as","21":"just … is","23":"flesh","24":"of a sin offering"},"g":[[0,2,"אם כך","a"],[3,6,"הרי התורה הכשירה אותם","a"],[7,9,"הוא אומר להם","a"],[9,10,"לי עצמי, לשיטתי","a"],[10,12,"התורה הכשירה אותו","a"],[12,13,"לשיטתכם","a"],[13,16,"הודו לי על כל פנים","a"],[20,21,"נחשב","a"],[21,23,"כמו שהוא","a"]]},{"k":"e58a9e6e7ea8","n":6,"p":[[0,1,"And the Rabbis,"],[1,2,"Here,"],[2,3,"are repulsive,"],[3,4,"there,"],[4,6,"are not repulsive"]],"w":{"0":"And the Rabbis","1":"Here","2":"are repulsive","3":"there","4":"not","5":"are … repulsive"},"g":[[0,1,"וחכמים","a"],[1,2,"כאן","a"],[2,3,"מאוסים","a"],[3,4,"שם","a"],[4,6,"אינם מאוסים","a"]]},{"k":"50eca17aa235","n":34,"p":[[1,2,"limbs"],[2,5,"with limbs of blemished"],[5,8,"Rabbi Eliezer says:"],[8,16,"if the hea